# L §5.5 example axis, copied whole; "A rule may test it: when ul05_cut == floor."  Fan-out: "An ask evaluates
# every combination of the axes its evaluation reads ... It prints one line per distinct result"; on a line an
# axis prints the options that give it, and the line's reading: entry names them (§8.2).  Lines are ordered by
# the axes' options in declaration order (L §5.18 Output).  Under floor the rule gives round(x, 1, floor) of
# 10.5 = 10 (L §7.2 floor: toward −∞); under exact the value 10.5 itself.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

source s "s"

axis ul05_cut
  floor "the cut rounds down to whole złoty"
  exact "no rounding is stated"

input x: num
input one: num

def cut_x: num at reader
  rule base = x
  rule floored beats base = round(x, one, floor) when ul05_cut == floor

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2016-01-01
  x = 10.5
  one = 1

ask q1: cut_x law 2016-03-01
=== expect
q1 [ul05_cut = floor]: 10
  reading: ul05_cut = floor
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-03-01
q1 [ul05_cut = exact]: 10.5
  reading: ul05_cut = exact
  law date 2016-03-01, cut 2016-03-01
